From 7f1be0966c8807a3bfd48163b12cea7cda29f658 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:39:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] freedreno/a5xx: partition the colour cache for the part's SP
 cores

RB_CCU_CNTL splits the colour cache between the SP cores, and freedreno
always programs the four-core a530 partition, for GMEM rendering and for
bypass alike. Every other a5xx part has one or two cores, so the cache
is carved up for cores that do not exist.

Describe RB_CCU_CNTL's offset and cache size fields, which are similar
to a6xx's COLOR_OFFSET, COLOR_CACHE_SIZE, DEPTH_OFFSET and
DEPTH_CACHE_SIZE, only at lower bit positions, and program each part's
own GMEM partition with them. Derive the bypass one from the SP core
count, which gives each core 32 units. This also covers the
bypass write before an LRZ clear.

Fixes: 224b26728296 ("freedreno/a5xx: enable a510")
Fixes: 07e1233c6157 ("freedreno: Enable Adreno 508, 509 and 512")
Fixes: dc6f7045665e ("freedreno: Enable A506")
Fixes: afb7b17fddca ("freedreno: Enable A505")
